{"ref":"BDB, חֶלְאָה","hw":"חֶלְאָה","html":"† I. <big>[<span dir=\"rtl\">חֶלְאָה</span>]</big>  <strong>n.f. rust (</strong>perhaps as <em>filth</em> v. supr.<strong>)</strong>—<span dir=\"rtl\">חֶלְאָתָהּ</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 24:6\" href=\"/Ezekiel.24.6\">Ez 24:6</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 24:12\" href=\"/Ezekiel.24.12\">12</a> + v <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 24:11\" href=\"/Ezekiel.24.11\">11</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 24:12\" href=\"/Ezekiel.24.12\">12</a> (del. Co intern. grounds) + v <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 24:6\" href=\"/Ezekiel.24.6\">6</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">חֶלְאָתָהֿ</span> (cf. Ges<sup>§ 91, 1; R. 2</sup>) <em>rust</em> on metal pot, symbol of impurity of Jerusalem.","next":"BDB, חֶלְאָה²","prev":"BDB, חלא"}